# ── ADDED THE DAY THIS PROJECT JOINED THE REPO (19 Aug) ──────────────────────
# together-city-mobile/ lived in .git/info/exclude — a LOCAL rule, on one
# machine, invisible to the remote and to everybody else. That is why the felt
# app icon could be written to disk and then refuse to be committed. The folder
# is tracked now, and these two lines are what had to be true first.

# 141 MB. A snapshot of the web build's public/ folder, taken once to seed www/.
# GitHub refuses any single file over 100 MB, so without this line `git add`
# on this folder cannot succeed at all — it is not a preference, it is the
# blocker.
_public-assets.tar.gz

# Built APKs. sideload/ holds the hand-rolled build's SOURCES — its manifest,
# its assets — and those stay tracked. The .apk it produces is output, and a
# binary that changes wholesale on every build is the worst thing a history can
# carry. The download the site serves is versioned in the web project, at
# together-city-react/public/downloads/, which is where a shipped artifact
# belongs.
sideload/*.apk
